    "billPage": 0,
    "chapter": 0,
    "lineEnd": 0,
    "lineStart": 0,
    "memoText": "\n \n                         VETO MESSAGE - No. 188\n \nTO THE SENATE:\n \nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n \nSenate Bill Number 5941, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to  amend the mental hygiene law, in relation to requiring\n      monthly reports of community investments and the impact  on  inpa-\n      tient census\"\n \n    NOT APPROVED\n \n  This  bill  would  require  the  Commissioner  of the Office of Mental\nHealth (OMH) to  provide  monthly  status  reports  regarding  community\ninvestments  and  the  impact on inpatient census to the Legislature, as\nwell as posting the reports on OMH's public website.\n \n  OMH has provided reports of this nature on  a  monthly  basis  to  the\nLegislature  from  the  2015  Fiscal  Year  to the 2019 Fiscal Year as a\nresult of agreements reached during annual Budget negotiations.    Addi-\ntionally, OMH has posted State Psychiatric Center (PC) operating charac-\nteristics and performance measures at the facility level; information on\nfunding  and  utilization levels for all programs funded by reinvestment\nof State PC reduction savings; and reinvestments of the State  share  of\nMedicaid for inpatient hospital bed reductions on its public website.\n \n  The Legislature did not request provisions for the continued reporting\nof this information nor include funding for these reports as part of the\nFiscal  Year  2020  Enacted  Budget. In addition, the chaptering of this\nlegislation would make this a permanent reporting  requirement,  placing\nan  undue  burden to produce a report that may not have relevancy in the\nfuture.\n \n  For these reasons, I am constrained to veto the  bill  at  this  time.\nHowever,  the  Legislature could address this proposal in the context of\nfuture State Budget negotiations. In the meantime, adequate  information\nexists publicly on the OMH website to achieve these goals.\n \n  The bill is disapproved.                    (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n \n                               __________\n",
